[Fact:hawkwind:Dedicated To Hawkwind]
The game's welcome text, stored tokenised at the start of #R$75CE, dedicates
Blizzard Pass to the band Hawkwind. See also <a href="https://www.mobygames.com/game/14692/blizzard-pass/"
  rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">MobyGames</a>.

[Fact:source:Leftover Source Code]
When the game was saved, part of Alan Cox's assembler source was still in
memory. At #R$B74F you can read lines 1090 to 1140 of it, including
<code>CP (HL)</code> and <code>JR Z,found</code>.
<a href="https://tcrf.net/Blizzard_Pass_(ZX_Spectrum)"
  rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">The Cutting Room Floor</a> lists the same
fragments.

[Fact:carried:A Ghost In The Inventory]
The copy at #R$600F moves #N($0100,$04,$04) bytes from #R$B6A8, running on
past the source leftovers into #R$B798 and the start of the picture at
#R$B79C. Its #N$FD byte lands on object slot #N($F4), so the "drop everything"
routine at #R$6A68 treats that slot as carried and writes the current room to
#R$5DCA(#N$5EBE), a slot no object uses.

[Fact:abermud:Back In AberMUD]
Alan Cox later reused Blizzard Pass as a zone in AberMUD, where the
scenario credits that section "(C)1988 Alan Cox". Sources:
<a href="https://www.mobygames.com/game/14692/blizzard-pass/trivia/"
  rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">MobyGames trivia</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AberMUD"
  rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">Wikipedia</a>. In the AberMUD version you
freeze to death within about twenty moves unless you find warmth
(<a href="https://abermud.tripod.com/news10.html"
  rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">AberMUD news</a>).

[Fact:loading:128K Only]
Blizzard Pass needs a 128K Spectrum, and its loader uses OUT 32765,23 to
page memory before loading. It was sold with H.A.R.D. by Tynesoft in 1986
and on Tynesoft's 128 &ndash; 4 Pack in 1987. Source:
<a href="https://spectrumcomputing.co.uk/entry/6016"
  rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">Spectrum Computing</a>.

[Fact:banks:Bank 7 Unused]
The loader pages bank 7 only so 128 BASIC can load the game. The game is
copied into banks 6, 3 and 0 and never selects bank 7 again. The top of
bank 0 still holds 128 BASIC leftovers from #R$FF18, including a fragment of
its character set from #N$FF58.

[Fact:signature:ADVENTURE]
The nine bytes at #R$676E spell ADVENTURE, but the key routine and the
random condition overwrite them and use the first byte as scratch space.

[Fact:riddle:Red To Red]
System message #R$7E26(#N$81CF) holds the riddle "red to red, wave to wave, thus
pass away from cave to cave. Seek the sorcerors doom, near the once wet
place, not a room. Seek the hidden way in the dungeons. He is across the pit
of fire bridged by a sceptre. Aranus last wiza...." It breaks off mid-word,
and "sorcerors" is spelled that way in the game.

[Fact:leftovers:Leftovers]
#R$6B59 is an unused, older version of the end of the action table, the
redraw routine and the glyph buffer, and #R$B66C is an unused copy of the
first #N$3C bytes of the object list.
